<title>SINGAPORE: WBL 1st-half net profit rises 66.8 pct.</title>
<headline>WBL 1st-half net profit rises 66.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    15.78  vs  9.46</p>
<p>    Dividend (percent)		   3.00  vs   3.00</p>
<p>    Group share (cts)		   13.90  vs   8.30</p>
<p>    Group share fully diluted (cts) 13.80  vs   8.30</p>
<p>    Turnover			     381.14  vs 357.02</p>
<p>    Investment income		    2.05  vs   0.55</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	2.17  vs   2.12</p>
<p>    Interest expense		    11.91  vs  11.93</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortisation	 13.58  vs  12.95</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			27.66  vs  19.05</p>
<p>    Income from associates	     7.47  vs   2.35</p>
<p>    Tax				     13.87  vs   8.85</p>
<p>    Minorities		    (loss) 5.49  vs   3.08 (loss)</p>
<p>    Extraordinary items	 (gain) 6.19  vs   0.21 (gain)</p>
<p>    Dividend pay date:	   August 27, 1997</p>
<p>    Last day books open:	 August 11, 1997</p>
<p>Note - WBL Corp Ltd is a diversified company involved many areas including construction, engineering, agrobusiness, manufacturing, electronics and property.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
